::notice file=.github/workflows/deploy.yml,line=6,col=9,title=EG012 ci-secret-undocumented::workflows use variable DEPLOY_ENABLED, but no template or schema documents it%0A%0AWhy: Whoever sets up a fork, a new environment or a new repository has to discover DEPLOY_ENABLED by reading workflow files; a missing one usually shows up as a failed deploy.%0A%0AFix: Document it: add `DEPLOY_ENABLED=` to .env.example with a comment such as `# CI: set in GitHub → Settings → Secrets and variables → Actions (Variables tab)`, or declare it under `variables:` in .envguard.yaml.
::notice file=.github/workflows/deploy.yml,line=13,col=27,title=EG012 ci-secret-undocumented::workflows use secret DEPLOY_KEY, but no template or schema documents it%0A%0AWhy: Whoever sets up a fork, a new environment or a new repository has to discover DEPLOY_KEY by reading workflow files; a missing one usually shows up as a failed deploy.%0A%0AFix: Document it: add `DEPLOY_KEY=` to .env.example with a comment such as `# CI: set in GitHub → Settings → Secrets and variables → Actions (Secrets tab)`, or declare it under `variables:` in .envguard.yaml.
::notice file=.github/workflows/deploy.yml,line=15,col=23,title=EG012 ci-secret-undocumented::workflows use variable AWS_DEPLOY_REGION, but no template or schema documents it%0A%0AWhy: Whoever sets up a fork, a new environment or a new repository has to discover AWS_DEPLOY_REGION by reading workflow files; a missing one usually shows up as a failed deploy.%0A%0AFix: Document it: add `AWS_DEPLOY_REGION=` to .env.example with a comment such as `# CI: set in GitHub → Settings → Secrets and variables → Actions (Variables tab)`, or declare it under `variables:` in .envguard.yaml.
